/* A definite integral assumes facts about its variable and forgets them
   again.  forget() must remove the fact of its own context: taking the
   first matching fact of any context, one runner's integral deleted the
   assumptions of another runner integrating over the same variable, whose
   integral then came back unevaluated -- measured, 10 to 28 of 48 to 96
   parallel integrals of sqrt(x+1/x-2) over [0, 1] (GitHub issue #94). */

(forget_int(i) := integrate(sqrt(x + 1/x - 2), x, 0, 1),
 forget_int(0));
