/* sublis keeps its substitutions in a table of each call's own.  Kept on
   the property lists of the symbols, which all threads share, concurrent
   calls substituting for the same symbol lost each other's entries and
   left the symbol in place: measured on SBCL and CCL, every run of the
   48 elements below missed substitutions, and parallel eigenvectors()
   returned eigenvectors still carrying %r1, because every runner
   substitutes for that same symbol (GitHub issue #79).

   First, the behaviour the table has to keep: substitution is
   simultaneous, the first equation for a symbol wins, false is a value
   like any other, function names are replaced, and a substituted lambda
   is applied. */
(kill(all), 0);

0$

